//! The free-form date/time parser (`strtotime()`, `DateTime::__construct()`, `DateTime::modify()`), the format
//! parser (`DateTime::createFromFormat()`), zone-string parsing and `timelib_fill_holes()` (port of
//! `PHPSRC/ext/date/lib/parse_date.re`).
//!
//! The scanner itself (`scanner`) is generated by re2rust 4.1 from `scanner.re`, a copy of timelib's
//! `parse_date.re` whose regular-expression definitions and rules are verbatim and whose C actions are
//! translated to Rust (see `research/timelib-port/README.md` and `tools/regen_scanner.sh`). This module holds
//! the scanner state and the C helper functions the actions call, ported one to one. The helpers walk
//! NUL-terminated byte strings exactly like the C `const char **ptr` code, including its behaviour around
//! embedded NUL bytes.

